+++ b/crates/encounters/src/skin.rs
@@ -0,0 +1,649 @@
+//! The slack skin: encounter certificates that absorb kicks, and are re-set up only when a
+//! drift budget breaks (the Verlet-skin idea, in the certificate's own units).
+//!
+//! A pair's certificate is its [`Section`]s (arcs + windows, built once by
+//! [`crate::pairs::sections_pad`]) plus the integer first-hit query that jumps to the next
+//! passage whose offset lies in the window. Re-building it after every kick is the encounter
+//! engine's dominant cost (92% of per-kick evals on the belt; lab 20261006-0737-components).
+//! Between re-setups the kicks move each body's Binet point and period by a bounded amount,
+//! and a *widened* copy of the stored certificate stays a superset for the current orbits.
+//! The exact check always runs on the current orbits, so a superset certificate cannot miss
+//! an encounter; it can only over-propose.
+//!
+//! # Exactness argument (why each widening term is there)
+//!
+//! Track per body: `dbin` = accumulated |δ(Binet point)| and `dper` = accumulated |δperiod|
+//! since the certificate's anchors (both are sums of absolute increments, hence upper bounds).
+//! Let δ = (dbin_i − b0_i) + (dbin_j − b0_j) and dp = the same for periods (ticks). At query
+//! time the trigger below guarantees δ < s (the skin width) and dp < its anchor sum.
+//!
+//! 1. **Arcs (which longitudes).** u(θ) = U + V cos θ + W sin θ is *affine* in the Binet
+//!    point, so |Δu_now(θ) − Δu_setup(θ)| ≤ δ for every θ. Sections are built with the
+//!    tolerance eps_u + s while the trigger fires at δ ≥ s/2, so every longitude where the
+//!    current orbits are within eps_u of each other — a necessary condition for an encounter,
+//!    with eps_u's own 1.5 margin absorbing eps_u's drift under kicks — lies inside a stored
+//!    arc. The arc times `di`/`dj` cover the padded arc, hence cover any encounter longitude.
+//!
+//! 2. **Window edges (which passages).** A section is an integer circle rotation with the
+//!    *stored* periods: offset s_l = (c0 − l·P_j) mod P_i. With the current periods the true
+//!    conjunction offsets differ by at most l·|ΔP_j| + l·(P_j/P_i)·|ΔP_i| ticks after l
+//!    revolutions of j, so both edges widen by W = 1.5·(revs + 1)·dp (revs = revolutions to
+//!    the horizon; the 1.5 covers the P_j/P_i leverage).
+//!
+//! 3. **Window width (the tangential term; q-skin named it, mis-sized it).** At a transversal
+//!    crossing the window is w ≈ ρ/c with c = |v_i × v_j|/|v_i − v_j|. Writing the crossing
+//!    angle α = q/u (q = sqrt(r² − ΔU²), the transversality; tan of the flight-path-angle
+//!    difference is |dΔu/dθ|/u = q/u at the crossing) and the speed mismatch β ≈ |ΔU|/2
+//!    (vis-viva at the common radius), c = V·α/hypot(α, β), so
+//!    w = (ρ/V)·sqrt(1 + (β/α)²). Drift moves q by at most 2rδ/q and with q² = (r − |ΔU|)·
+//!    (r + |ΔU|) = g·(2r − g) ≥ g·r this is dq/q ≤ 2δ/g, where g = r − |ΔU| is the pair's
+//!    tangency gap. In the binding regime (near-tangential, β ≳ α) the width scales as 1/q,
+//!    so the stored width must be *inverted*, not padded:
+//!        w_now ≤ w_setup / (1 − 2δ/g).
+//!    Transversal pairs (β ≪ α) have c ≈ V and are insensitive; for them g ≈ r and the same
+//!    formula is a loose bound, which costs only proposals. When 2δ/g ≥ 1/2 the geometry is
+//!    too stale to widen and the pair is re-set up instead (TANGENCY reset): the skin's
+//!    width is decided by the pair's own tangency, not by a global s.
+//!
+//! 3b. **Crossing-longitude drift (the term q-skin missed).** The crossing longitude moves
+//!    by up to δ·(2/q + 1/r) rad (then time at the Kepler rate r²/√p), shifting the window
+//!    *centre*; both edges (and the check-interval stretch) widen by it, capped at the
+//!    section's arc traversal (the encounter longitude stays inside the padded arc, term 1,
+//!    so beyond the cap nothing new can be proposed). Measured at ε = 1e-4: every miss sat
+//!    at exactly this scale, 2–4× past the old widened window.
+//!
+//! 4. **Check interval.** The encounter time lies within both bodies' passages across the
+//!    stored arc; the caps stretch by the period-drift fraction 2ΔP_j/P_j plus W/TICKS (the
+//!    widened edges in time), and the bracketing step count scales with the stretched
+//!    interval (`kscale`).
+//!
+//! 5. **Saturation.** A widened window that would swallow a quarter of the stored period is
+//!    not a window any more: re-set up (SATURATION reset).
+//!
+//! 6. **The empty certificate.** `numeric_window` can prove the pair *cannot* encounter at
+//!    its setup elements (a None hull). That proof has no slack to widen — any kick breaks
+//!    it — so an empty certificate re-proves at the first maintenance pass after any drift.
+//!    Kicks land at segment starts and elements are constant within a segment, so the
+//!    re-proof precedes that segment's query; nothing can hide in between. This was the
+//!    last miss at ε = 1e-4: adjacent belt indices whose "never" proof was blown by the
+//!    kicks between two drift-trigger resets.
+//!
+//! What is empirical: the 1.1 safety on fresh Cross windows, the 1.5 edge factor, and the
+//! constant 2 in 2δ/g — each derived above at the order-of-magnitude level and held by the
+//! tests (zero misses against the crate's independent conservative-advancement truth across
+//! kick sizes ε = 1e-8…1e-4) and by the killed literal control (cone pad only: 102/159 belt
+//! encounters missed at ε = 1e-4; lab 20261002-0539-q-skin).
+
+use crate::kepler::{Body, TICKS};
+use crate::method::{run_section, Stats};
+use crate::pairs::{cone_gap, eps_u, sections_pad, Kind, Section, Sorted};
+use std::collections::HashMap;
+
+/// Safety factor on fresh linear Cross windows (the crate's `SAFETY`).
+pub const SAFETY: f64 = 1.1;
+/// Horizon of the query done at (re)set up: the pair's next events are certified this far.
+pub const HQ: f64 = 100.0 * std::f64::consts::TAU;
+/// Segment length: kicks are quantized to segment boundaries; elements are constant within.
+pub const SEG: f64 = std::f64::consts::TAU;
+/// Edge-widening leverage factor (term 2).
+const EDGE: f64 = 1.5;
+/// Tangency saturation: widen while 2δ/g < this, else re-set up (term 3).
+const TANGENCY: f64 = 0.5;
+
+/// `always` re-set ups every kicked body's pairs each pass (r8 v3's behaviour, the control);
+/// `skin` defers through the widening above.
+#[derive(Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq, Debug)]
+pub enum Mode {
+    Always,
+    Skin,
+}
+
+#[derive(Clone, Debug)]
+pub struct Cert {
+    /// Accumulated |δBinet| and |δperiod| anchors at setup, per body (i, j).
+    pub b0: [f64; 2],
+    pub p0: [f64; 2],
+    /// Setup time (time units).
+    pub t0: f64,
+    /// Tangency gap g of the pair at setup (Binet units); term 3's denominator.
+    pub g: f64,
+    /// Transversality q = sqrt(r² − ΔU²) and transverse separation r (Binet units).
+    pub q: f64,
+    pub rb: f64,
+    /// Kepler time per unit angle at the pair's widest: r_max²/√p_min (time units per rad).
+    pub rate: f64,
+    pub secs: Vec<Section>,
+}
+
+#[derive(Default, Clone, Copy, Debug)]
+pub struct Counters {
+    pub kicks: u64,
+    pub scans: u64,
+    pub cone_tests: u64,
+    /// Setups by origin: new pairs, the drift trigger, saturation, tangency.
+    pub setups: u64,
+    pub setup_new: u64,
+    pub trig_resets: u64,
+    pub sat_resets: u64,
+    pub tangency_resets: u64,
+    /// Empty certificates re-proven (term 6: a None window has no slack).
+    pub empty_resets: u64,
+    /// Certificates sampled per pass and how many were false candidates at query time.
+    pub cert_samples: u64,
+    pub false_cand: u64,
+    pub events: u64,
+    pub st: Stats,
+}
+
+/// One doll of bodies under the skin.
+pub struct Skin {
+    pub b: Vec<Body>,
+    pub rho: f64,
+    /// Skin width s (Binet units).
+    pub s: f64,
+    pub mode: Mode,
+    pub dbin: Vec<f64>,
+    pub dper: Vec<f64>,
+    scan_anchor: Vec<f64>,
+    /// Read-only outside the crate: diagnosis and tests inspect stored certificates.
+    pub certs: HashMap<(u32, u32), Cert>,
+    pub c: Counters,
+}
+
+fn key(i: u32, j: u32) -> (u32, u32) {
+    (i.min(j), i.max(j))
+}
+
+fn dist3(a: [f64; 3], b: [f64; 3]) -> f64 {
+    let d = [a[0] - b[0], a[1] - b[1], a[2] - b[2]];
+    (d[0] * d[0] + d[1] * d[1] + d[2] * d[2]).sqrt()
+}
+
+impl Skin {
+    pub fn new(b: Vec<Body>, rho: f64, s: f64, mode: Mode) -> Self {
+        let n = b.len();
+        Skin {
+            b,
+            rho,
+            s,
+            mode,
+            dbin: vec![0.0; n],
+            dper: vec![0.0; n],
+            scan_anchor: vec![0.0; n],
+            certs: HashMap::new(),
+            c: Counters::default(),
+        }
+    }
+
+    /// Full (re)setup of one pair: padded sections plus the horizon query. The expensive unit.
+    fn setup(&mut self, i: u32, j: u32, t: f64) {
+        let (i, j) = (i.min(j), i.max(j));
+        let bi = self.b[i as usize];
+        let bj = self.b[j as usize];
+        let pad = if self.mode == Mode::Skin { self.s } else { 0.0 };
+        let mut secs = sections_pad(&bi, &bj, self.rho, SAFETY, pad, &mut self.c.st.evals);
+        let mut ev = Vec::new();
+        for sec in &secs {
+            run_section(&bi, &bj, sec, self.rho, t, t + HQ, &mut self.c.st, &mut ev);
+        }
+        self.c.events += ev.len() as u64;
+        secs.shrink_to_fit();
+        // Term 3's denominator: the tangency gap at setup, from the cone coordinates.
+        let (ai, aj) = (bi.binet(), bj.binet());
+        let r = (ai[1] - aj[1]).hypot(ai[2] - aj[2]);
+        let g = (r - (ai[0] - aj[0]).abs()).max(1e-300);
+        let q = (r * r - (ai[0] - aj[0]) * (ai[0] - aj[0])).max(0.0).sqrt().max(1e-300);
+        let rate = bi.rmax().max(bj.rmax()).powi(2) / bi.p.min(bj.p).sqrt();
+        let cert = Cert {
+            b0: [self.dbin[i as usize], self.dbin[j as usize]],
+            p0: [self.dper[i as usize], self.dper[j as usize]],
+            t0: t,
+            g,
+            q,
+            rb: r,
+            rate,
+            secs,
+        };
+        self.certs.insert((i, j), cert);
+        self.c.setups += 1;
+    }
+
+    /// The certificate's sections widened for the drift accumulated since setup (terms 2–4).
+    /// `None`: saturated (term 5) or tangency-stale (term 3) — the caller re-setups.
+    pub fn widened(&self, cert: &Cert, i: u32, j: u32, t1: f64) -> Option<Vec<Section>> {
+        let dpi = self.dper[i as usize] - cert.p0[0];
+        let dpj = self.dper[j as usize] - cert.p0[1];
+        let dp = (dpi + dpj).max(0.0);
+        let drift = (self.dbin[i as usize] - cert.b0[0]) + (self.dbin[j as usize] - cert.b0[1]);
+        let pj = self.b[j as usize].period as f64;
+        let pi = self.b[i as usize].period as i64;
+        let revs = (((t1 - cert.t0) * TICKS / pj).max(1.0) + 1.0) * EDGE;
+        let w = (revs * dp).ceil() as i64;
+        let f = 2.0 * dp / pj;
+        let wt = w as f64 / TICKS;
+        // Term 3a: the width inversion, for Cross windows only (w ≈ ρ/c scales as 1/q near
+        // tangency). Wide and Full windows are rigorous hulls/spreads, and their pairs
+        // (co-orbital, near-identical) have g ≈ 0 by construction: widening or resetting
+        // them on 2δ/g would degenerate the skin there.
+        let has_cross = cert.secs.iter().any(|s| s.kind == Kind::Cross);
+        let scale = if !has_cross || drift <= 0.0 {
+            1.0
+        } else {
+            let x = 2.0 * drift / cert.g;
+            if x >= TANGENCY {
+                return None;
+            }
+            1.0 / (1.0 - x)
+        };
+        // Term 3b: the crossing-longitude drift. The crossing longitude θ_c solves
+        // cos(θ_c − θ₀) = −ΔU/r with θ₀ = atan2(ΔW, ΔV), so a total Binet drift δ moves
+        // θ_c by at most δ·(r + |ΔU|)/(r·q) + δ/r ≤ δ·(2/q + 1/r) rad (q the
+        // transversality, r the transverse separation), and θ₀ drift also slides the arc's
+        // reference longitude itself. At the Kepler rate dt = r²/√p · dθ (stored as `rate`
+        // for the pair's widest radius), the window *centre* shifts by up to
+        //   wx = δ · (2/q + 1/r) · r_max²/√p_min
+        // time units — while the edge term (term 2) covers only the rotation-lattice drift
+        // l·ΔP. This is the term q-skin missed at ε = 1e-4: its misses sat 2–4× beyond its
+        // widened window, at exactly this scale. Capped at the section's arc traversal: an
+        // encounter longitude cannot leave the padded arc (term 1), so beyond the cap the
+        // widened window already covers every passage whose check interval can hold the
+        // pair. Full sections (q ≈ 0, spread windows) skip it: their offsets drift by the
+        // period term alone.
+        let wx = if cert.q > 1e-12 {
+            let raw = drift * (2.0 / cert.q + 1.0 / cert.rb) * cert.rate;
+            let mut cap = 0.0f64;
+            for sec in &cert.secs {
+                cap = cap.max(sec.di.0 + sec.di.1 + sec.dj.0 + sec.dj.1);
+            }
+            if cap > 1e-9 { raw.min(cap) } else { 0.0 }
+        } else {
+            0.0
+        };
+        let wxt = (wx * TICKS).ceil() as i64;
+        let mut out = Vec::with_capacity(cert.secs.len());
+        for sec in &cert.secs {
+            let mut s2 = sec.clone();
+            if s2.w1 + s2.w2 + 2 * (w + wxt) > pi / 4 {
+                return None;
+            }
+            if s2.kind == Kind::Cross {
+                s2.w1 = (s2.w1 as f64 * scale).ceil() as i64 + w + wxt;
+                s2.w2 = (s2.w2 as f64 * scale).ceil() as i64 + w + wxt;
+            } else {
+                s2.w1 += w + wxt;
+                s2.w2 += w + wxt;
+            }
+            // The drifted conjunction lies within ±(wt + wx) of the proposed offset: the
+            // check interval must stretch with it, and its bracketing resolution with the
+            // interval.
+            let span = s2.di.0 + s2.di.1 + s2.dj.0 + s2.dj.1;
+            let span = if span > 1e-9 { span } else { pj / TICKS };
+            let stretch = wt + wx;
+            s2.kscale = 1.0 + 4.0 * stretch / span;
+            s2.di = (s2.di.0 * (1.0 + f) + stretch, s2.di.1 * (1.0 + f) + stretch);
+            s2.dj = (s2.dj.0 * (1.0 + f) + stretch, s2.dj.1 * (1.0 + f) + stretch);
+            out.push(s2);
+        }
+        Some(out)
+    }
+
+    /// One body's range scan: fresh certs for pairs entering the padded cone, drops for pairs
+    /// that left it. The pad and the scan anchor (s/4 per body) make the padded test at scan
+    /// time a superset of the exact test until the next scan: cone_gap is 2-Lipschitz in the
+    /// Binet difference, and between scans each body drifts < s/4 + one segment of kicks
+    /// (`reach_extra`, passed by the driver).
+    fn scan(&mut self, sorted: &Sorted, i: u32, t: f64, reach_extra: f64) {
+        if self.mode == Mode::Always {
+            let drop: Vec<(u32, u32)> = self.certs.keys().copied().filter(|&k| k.0 == i || k.1 == i).collect();
+            for k in drop {
+                self.certs.remove(&k);
+            }
+        }
+        let bi = self.b[i as usize];
+        let pad = if self.mode == Mode::Always { 0.0 } else { self.s };
+        let (lo, hi) = sorted.range(bi.binet()[0], sorted.reach(&bi) + reach_extra + pad);
+        let mut drop_later = Vec::new();
+        let mut setup_later = Vec::new();
+        for &(_, j) in &sorted.order[lo..hi] {
+            if j == i {
+                continue;
+            }
+            self.c.cone_tests += 1;
+            let bj = self.b[j as usize];
+            if cone_gap(&bi, &bj) < eps_u(&bi, &bj, self.rho) + pad {
+                if !self.certs.contains_key(&key(i, j)) {
+                    setup_later.push(j);
+                }
+            } else if self.certs.contains_key(&key(i, j)) {
+                drop_later.push(j);
+            }
+        }
+        self.c.scans += 1;
+        for j in setup_later {
+            self.c.setup_new += 1;
+            self.setup(i, j, t);
+        }
+        for j in drop_later {
+            self.certs.remove(&key(i, j));
+        }
+    }
+
+    /// A kick at time `t`: `a` scaled by `frac`, e, ϖ and mean longitude continuous.
+    pub fn kick(&mut self, i: usize, t: f64, frac: f64) {
+        let old = self.b[i];
+        let lam = old.mean_anomaly(t) + old.pom;
+        let a_new = old.a * (1.0 + frac);
+        let n_new = a_new.powf(-1.5);
+        let new = Body::new(a_new, old.e, old.pom, lam - n_new * t);
+        self.dbin[i] += dist3(new.binet(), old.binet());
+        self.dper[i] += (new.period as f64 - old.period as f64).abs();
+        self.b[i] = new;
+        self.c.kicks += 1;
+    }
+
+    /// Initial pass: build every padded-candidate pair once.
+    pub fn initial_scan(&mut self) {
+        let sorted = Sorted::new(&self.b, self.rho);
+        let pad = if self.mode == Mode::Always { 0.0 } else { self.s };
+        let mut setup_later = Vec::new();
+        for (k, &(u, i)) in sorted.order.iter().enumerate() {
+            let bi = self.b[i as usize];
+            let (lo, hi) = sorted.range(u, sorted.reach(&bi) + pad);
+            for &(_, j) in &sorted.order[lo.max(k + 1)..hi] {
+                self.c.cone_tests += 1;
+                let bj = self.b[j as usize];
+                if cone_gap(&bi, &bj) < eps_u(&bi, &bj, self.rho) + pad {
+                    setup_later.push((i, j));
+                }
+            }
+        }
+        self.c.scans += self.b.len() as u64;
+        for (i, j) in setup_later {
+            self.c.setup_new += 1;
+            self.setup(i, j, 0.0);
+        }
+    }
+
+    /// One segment: apply `kicks` at t0, re-scan kicked bodies whose scan anchor broke, then
+    /// the maintenance pass (triggers, widening, the short query over [t0, t1]). Events land
+    /// in `out` as (i, j, t, dmin). `reach_extra` bounds one segment of Binet drift per body
+    /// (the sorted index is rebuilt once per segment).
+    pub fn advance(&mut self, t0: f64, t1: f64, kicks: &[(usize, f64)], reach_extra: f64, out: &mut Vec<(u32, u32, f64, f64)>) {
+        for &(i, frac) in kicks {
+            self.kick(i, t0, frac);
+        }
+        let sorted = Sorted::new(&self.b, self.rho);
+        let mut done = vec![false; self.b.len()];
+        for &(i, _) in kicks {
+            if done[i] {
+                continue;
+            }
+            done[i] = true;
+            if self.mode == Mode::Always || self.dbin[i] - self.scan_anchor[i] >= self.s / 4.0 {
+                self.scan_anchor[i] = self.dbin[i];
+                self.scan(&sorted, i as u32, t0, reach_extra);
+            }
+        }
+        let keys: Vec<(u32, u32)> = self.certs.keys().copied().collect();
+        for k in keys {
+            let (i, j) = k;
+            let (bi, bj) = (self.b[i as usize], self.b[j as usize]);
+            self.c.cert_samples += 1;
+            self.c.false_cand += (cone_gap(&bi, &bj) >= eps_u(&bi, &bj, self.rho)) as u64;
+            let (secs_empty, b0) = match self.certs.get(&k) {
+                Some(c) => (c.secs.is_empty(), c.b0),
+                None => continue,
+            };
+            let secs = match self.mode {
+                Mode::Always => self.certs.get(&k).map(|c| c.secs.clone()).unwrap_or_default(),
+                Mode::Skin => {
+                    // Term 6 first: a certificate with no sections is a *proof* that the
+                    // pair cannot encounter at its setup elements (numeric_window's None).
+                    // That proof has no slack to widen — any kick breaks it — so it re-proves
+                    // at the first pass after any drift. Kicks land at the segment start and
+                    // elements are constant within the segment, so the re-proof precedes the
+                    // query and no encounter can hide in between.
+                    let drift0 = (self.dbin[i as usize] - b0[0]) + (self.dbin[j as usize] - b0[1]);
+                    if secs_empty && drift0 > 0.0 {
+                        self.c.empty_resets += 1;
+                        self.setup(i, j, t0);
+                    }
+                    // The drift trigger next (keeps δ < s at query time for term 1).
+                    let drift = match self.certs.get(&k) {
+                        None => continue,
+                        Some(c) => (self.dbin[i as usize] - c.b0[0]) + (self.dbin[j as usize] - c.b0[1]),
+                    };
+                    if 2.0 * drift >= self.s {
+                        self.c.trig_resets += 1;
+                        self.setup(i, j, t0);
+                    }
+                    match self.certs.get(&k) {
+                        None => continue,
+                        Some(c) => match self.widened(c, i, j, t1) {
+                            Some(x) => x,
+                            None => {
+                                // Saturation or tangency staleness: which one? (term 5 vs 3;
+                                // term 3 applies to Cross certs only, as in `widened`.)
+                                let drift = (self.dbin[i as usize] - c.b0[0]) + (self.dbin[j as usize] - c.b0[1]);
+                                let has_cross = c.secs.iter().any(|s| s.kind == Kind::Cross);
+                                if has_cross && 2.0 * drift / c.g >= TANGENCY {
+                                    self.c.tangency_resets += 1;
+                                } else {
+                                    self.c.sat_resets += 1;
+                                }
+                                self.setup(i, j, t0);
+                                self.certs.get(&k).map(|c| c.secs.clone()).unwrap_or_default()
+                            }
+                        },
+                    }
+                }
+            };
+            let mut ev = Vec::new();
+            for sec in &secs {
+                run_section(&bi, &bj, sec, self.rho, t0, t1, &mut self.c.st, &mut ev);
+            }
+            self.c.events += ev.len() as u64;
+            for &(t, d) in &ev {
+                out.push((i, j, t, d));
+            }
+        }
+    }
+}
+
+#[cfg(test)]
+mod tests {
+    use super::*;
+    use std::f64::consts::TAU;
+    use crate::belt::{make_belt, Rng, Spec};
+    use crate::pairs::radial_pairs;
+    use crate::truth::truth_pair;
+
+    const TOL: f64 = 1e-3;
+
+    fn belt(n: usize, orbits: f64, seed: u64) -> (Vec<Body>, f64) {
+        let sp = Spec {
+            name: "skin-test".into(),
+            n,
+            sigma_e: 1e-2,
+            rho: 1e-4,
+            a_lo: 1.0,
+            a_hi: 1.5,
+            keys: 0,
+            seed,
+            orbits: 0.0,
+        };
+        (make_belt(&sp), orbits)
+    }
+
+    fn schedule(n: usize, segments: usize, kappa: f64, eps: f64, seed: u64) -> Vec<Vec<(usize, f64)>> {
+        let mut r = Rng(seed);
+        let whole = kappa.floor() as usize;
+        let frac = kappa - kappa.floor();
+        (0..segments)
+            .map(|_| {
+                let mut v = Vec::new();
+                for i in 0..n {
+                    let mut count = whole + (r.f64() < frac) as usize;
+                    while count > 0 {
+                        count -= 1;
+                        let sign = if r.f64() < 0.5 { -1.0 } else { 1.0 };
+                        v.push((i, eps * sign));
+                    }
+                }
+                v
+            })
+            .collect()
+    }
+
+    /// Independent per-segment truth: phase-reanchored copies, conservative advancement over
+    /// every radially overlapping pair (r8's truth construction, dense in time).
+    fn segment_truth(b: &[Body], rho: f64, t_a: f64, out: &mut Vec<(u32, u32, f64, f64)>) {
+        let shifted: Vec<Body> = b
+            .iter()
+            .map(|x| {
+                let lam = x.mean_anomaly(t_a) + x.pom;
+                Body::new(x.a, x.e, x.pom, lam)
+            })
+            .collect();
+        for &(i, j) in &radial_pairs(&shifted, rho) {
+            let mut v = Vec::new();
+            truth_pair(&shifted[i as usize], &shifted[j as usize], rho, SEG, &mut v, &mut Default::default());
+            for &(t, d) in &v {
+                out.push((i, j, t + t_a, d));
+            }
+        }
+    }
+
+    /// (missed, false) of a mode's per-segment events against the truth, per (segment, pair).
+    fn matchup(truth: &[(usize, u32, u32, f64)], got: &[(usize, u32, u32, f64)]) -> (u32, u32) {
+        use std::collections::HashMap;
+        let mut tby: HashMap<(usize, u32, u32), Vec<f64>> = HashMap::new();
+        for &(sg, i, j, t) in truth {
+            tby.entry((sg, i, j)).or_default().push(t);
+        }
+        let mut gby: HashMap<(usize, u32, u32), Vec<f64>> = HashMap::new();
+        for &(sg, i, j, t) in got {
+            gby.entry((sg, i, j)).or_default().push(t);
+        }
+        let missed = truth
+            .iter()
+            .filter(|&&(sg, i, j, t)| !gby.get(&(sg, i, j)).is_some_and(|v| v.iter().any(|&x| (x - t).abs() < TOL)))
+            .count() as u32;
+        let false_ = got
+            .iter()
+            .filter(|&&(sg, i, j, t)| !tby.get(&(sg, i, j)).is_some_and(|v| v.iter().any(|&x| (x - t).abs() < TOL)))
+            .count() as u32;
+        (missed, false_)
+    }
+
+    /// Run one mode over the kicked belt; events tagged with their segment.
+    fn run_mode(
+        bodies: &[Body],
+        rho: f64,
+        orbits: f64,
+        mode: Mode,
+        s: f64,
+        eps: f64,
+        seed: u64,
+    ) -> (Vec<(usize, u32, u32, f64)>, Skin) {
+        let segments = (orbits * TAU / SEG).round() as usize;
+        let sched = schedule(bodies.len(), segments, 0.3, eps, seed);
+        let mut w = Skin::new(bodies.to_vec(), rho, s, mode);
+        let reach_extra = 4.0 * eps * 1.3;
+        w.initial_scan();
+        let mut out = Vec::new();
+        for (sg, kicks) in sched.iter().enumerate() {
+            let t_a = sg as f64 * SEG;
+            let mut ev = Vec::new();
+            w.advance(t_a, t_a + SEG, kicks, reach_extra, &mut ev);
+            for &(i, j, t, _) in &ev {
+                out.push((sg, i, j, t));
+            }
+        }
+        (out, w)
+    }
+
+    fn truth_events(bodies: &[Body], rho: f64, orbits: f64, eps: f64, seed: u64) -> Vec<(usize, u32, u32, f64)> {
+        let segments = (orbits * TAU / SEG).round() as usize;
+        let sched = schedule(bodies.len(), segments, 0.3, eps, seed);
+        let mut cur = bodies.to_vec();
+        let mut truth = Vec::new();
+        for (sg, kicks) in sched.iter().enumerate() {
+            let t_a = sg as f64 * SEG;
+            for &(i, frac) in kicks {
+                let old = cur[i];
+                let lam = old.mean_anomaly(t_a) + old.pom;
+                let a_new = old.a * (1.0 + frac);
+                let n_new = a_new.powf(-1.5);
+                cur[i] = Body::new(a_new, old.e, old.pom, lam - n_new * t_a);
+            }
+            let mut seg_ev = Vec::new();
+            segment_truth(&cur, rho, t_a, &mut seg_ev);
+            for &(i, j, t, _) in &seg_ev {
+                truth.push((sg, i, j, t));
+            }
+        }
+        truth
+    }
+
+    /// The exactness contract at one kick size: the control (`always`, the crate's r8 v3
+    /// behaviour) and the skin both report every truth event and nothing else, and the
+    /// skin's empty certificates all sit at zero drift (term 6's invariant).
+    fn assert_exact(eps: f64) {
+        let (bodies, orbits) = belt(600, 12.0, 2026_1006 + eps.to_bits() % 7);
+        let rho = 1e-4;
+        let mut epsus: Vec<f64> = bodies.iter().map(|x| crate::pairs::eps_u(x, x, rho)).collect();
+        epsus.sort_by(|a, b| a.total_cmp(b));
+        let s = 4.0 * epsus[epsus.len() / 2];
+        let truth = truth_events(&bodies, rho, orbits, eps, 2026_1006);
+        assert!(!truth.is_empty(), "case with no events cannot defend exactness");
+        let (always, _) = run_mode(&bodies, rho, orbits, Mode::Always, 0.0, eps, 2026_1006);
+        let (skin, w) = run_mode(&bodies, rho, orbits, Mode::Skin, s, eps, 2026_1006);
+        let (m_a, f_a) = matchup(&truth, &always);
+        assert_eq!((m_a, f_a), (0, 0), "control (always) is not exact at eps {eps:e}: harness void");
+        let (m_s, f_s) = matchup(&truth, &skin);
+        assert_eq!((m_s, f_s), (0, 0), "skin missed/false events at eps {eps:e}");
+        for (k, cert) in &w.certs {
+            if cert.secs.is_empty() {
+                let drift = (w.dbin[k.0 as usize] - cert.b0[0]) + (w.dbin[k.1 as usize] - cert.b0[1]);
+                assert!(drift == 0.0, "empty certificate held drift {drift:e}: term 6 broken");
+            }
+        }
+    }
+
+    #[test]
+    fn exact_at_kick_eps_1e8() {
+        assert_exact(1e-8);
+    }
+
+    #[test]
+    fn exact_at_kick_eps_1e6() {
+        assert_exact(1e-6);
+    }
+
+    #[test]
+    fn exact_at_kick_eps_1e4() {
+        assert_exact(1e-4);
+    }
+
+    /// The economic point: at the plane's kick size the deferral cuts setups per kick
+    /// (deterministic counts, no timing).
+    #[test]
+    fn skin_cuts_setups_at_plane_kicks() {
+        let (bodies, orbits) = belt(600, 12.0, 2026_1007);
+        let rho = 1e-4;
+        let mut epsus: Vec<f64> = bodies.iter().map(|x| crate::pairs::eps_u(x, x, rho)).collect();
+        epsus.sort_by(|a, b| a.total_cmp(b));
+        let s = 4.0 * epsus[epsus.len() / 2];
+        let (_, wa) = run_mode(&bodies, rho, orbits, Mode::Always, 0.0, 1e-6, 2026_1007);
+        let (_, ws) = run_mode(&bodies, rho, orbits, Mode::Skin, s, 1e-6, 2026_1007);
+        let ka = wa.c.kicks as f64;
+        let ks = ws.c.kicks as f64;
+        let setups_a = wa.c.setups as f64 / ka;
+        let setups_s = ws.c.setups as f64 / ks;
+        assert!(
+            setups_s * 3.0 < setups_a,
+            "skin setups/kick {setups_s:.1} not a >=3x cut vs always {setups_a:.1}"
+        );
+    }
+}
